  "note": "Installs a ut_request.json (scaffold_tasks.py) and writes/qualifies its tasks, including mono_layer. Reads no profile evidence. Rebased onto geak-x ccc7427: preserve the upstream requirement for distinct replay-call IDs and compilation-variant links in kernel-ut/SKILL.md. c28 regression: host UID/GID Docker writers with writable AITER cache, shared-lock broker liveness across PID namespaces, read-only GPU flock handles, and native delivery verification before wave completion. Explicit resumes retain logs and renew attempts; finite request weights are enforced. Rebased onto geak-x f3d2153; keep the split driver's selective CPU copy of top-k score inputs, which already avoids copying unused comparison inputs (236ee03). Timing now batches shapes per immutable side/round, streams input factories, reports setup/input timing, and retains fresh-process A/A mode with separate resume identity. No user scheduling flag; retain timing errors and provide writable FlyDSL/AITER runtime caches. Current canonical UT receipts use the explicit ut_driver/source_snapshot/v1 delivery contract and full-report verification. Scoped wave freshness now uses native source/input hashes, not unrelated delivery/cache timestamps; explicit legacy snapshot contracts remain supported. Accept the driver's positive-infinite SQNR only in successful zero-error comparison diagnostics; preserve strict bounds, timing and other nonfinite rejection. Keep the default PyTorch HIP kernel cache on container-local Linux storage because ISA filenames with colons fail on some shared filesystems. Document full-set collective leases without nested locks and reserved rendezvous endpoints after real multi-rank startup failures. Resume rechecks outcomes after drain and reconciles valid deliveries interrupted before their terminal state was written. Lane and worker containers override the serving image's ENTRYPOINT (vLLM's is `vllm serve`). Task boundaries and the UT request are the brain's (brain/README.md); brain/tools was removed. The request-authoring contract (references/request-authoring.md) is owned here; Brain links to module inputs. ut_wave takes the deployment's serving.json (--serving) and GPU allocation (--gpus) as explicit inputs instead of looking beside the output directory; omitting --serving is refused unless --no-serving-env is recorded. Share evidence for Roofline is carried only with scaffold_tasks.py --selection. Merged geak-x 9699150d: absolute EVAL_DIR, run_task_entry.py as the lane's task entry, lane reports under run/. mono_layer UT template (menghongtao): generic rank harness + per-model rank_model.py, Muse Spark target/draft worked examples, per-model facts for the request author, rank_chain batched timing and --quick-timing.",
